    "probe_text": "The POST `/api/owners` endpoint is handled by `addOwner(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:162`. Here is everything it does, strictly in execution order. I've marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates the owner, persists, or logs).\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **Validation \u2014 authorization** (`@PreAuthorize`, line 160): caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else the request is rejected before any logic runs.\n\n## Inside `addOwner`\n\n2. **Validation \u2014 required fields** (`validateRequiredFields`, line 163): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked against its *normalized* form), `city`, and `telephone` must each be non-blank. All offending field names are collected and thrown together as `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n\n3. **Validation \u2014 postcode** (`validatePostcode`, line 164): only if a postcode is supplied (null/blank is allowed). It must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city has a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n4. **Side-effect \u2014 map DTO to entity** (line 166): `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n\n5. **Side-effect \u2014 normalize address** (line 167): trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word street abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`); stored on the owner.\n\n6. **Validation \u2014 future registration date** (`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`, line 168): if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today's server date, `FutureRegistrationDateException` (null is allowed).\n\n7. **Side-effect \u2014 set registration date to a business day** (lines 169\u2013172): effective date = supplied date or today; if it lands on Saturday/Sunday it rolls forward to Monday, and the result is stored.\n\n8. **Validation \u2014 daily owner limit** (`rejectWhenDailyLimitReached`, line 173): if 100 or more existing owners already carry that (business-day) registration date, `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n9. **Validation \u2014 city capacity** (`rejectWhenCityAtCapacity`, line 174): if the owner's city already holds 50 or more owners (case-insensitive), `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n10. **Side-effect + Validation \u2014 household** (`applyHousehold`, lines 175\u2013176): computes a deterministic `householdId` from normalized `lastName` + `postcode` and stores it on the owner (side-effect). Then, if any existing owner derives the same `householdId` **and** the request did *not* set `sharesHousehold=true`, `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n\n11. **Side-effect + Validation \u2014 normalize telephone** (line 177): strips spaces/dashes/brackets, forces E.164 (assuming `+61` and dropping a leading `0` when no `+`), and requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits with the correct national-number length for the country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); else `InvalidTelephoneException`. Normalized value stored.\n\n12. **Side-effect + Validation \u2014 normalize email** (line 178): null/blank \u2192 stored as null (allowed); otherwise trimmed and lower-cased, must match the email pattern (`InvalidEmailException`), and its domain must not be a disposable domain \u2014 `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` (`DisposableEmailException`). Normalized value stored.\n\n13. **Validation \u2014 duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`, line 179): builds `identityKey = telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + householdId` and rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (409) if any existing owner has the same full key.\n\n14. **Side-effect \u2014 assign customer code** (line 180): `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode range (else city table, else `UNKNOWN`), HASH8 = first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`.\n\n15. **Side-effect \u2014 assign membership number** (line 181): `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the registration-date year.\n\n16. **Side-effect \u2014 set namesake count** (line 182): counts existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), reflecting only pre-existing owners.\n\n17. **Side-effect \u2014 flag possible duplicate** (`flagPossibleDuplicate`, line 183): if not a declared household member, and an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<that owner's id>` (lowest id wins); otherwise sets them to `false`/null. Declared household members (`sharesHousehold=true`) are always `false`.\n\n18. **Side-effect \u2014 persist** (line 184): `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n\n19. **Side-effect \u2014 map to DTO** (line 185).\n\n20. **Side-effect \u2014 audit log** (lines 186\u2013188): `AUDIT` logger emits an \"owner created\" line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and membershipLevel.\n\n21. **Side-effect \u2014 Location header** (lines 189\u2013190): set to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n\n22. **Response** (line 191): `201 Created` with the owner DTO.\n\n### Notes on ordering worth flagging\n- The **required-field and postcode validations run first**, but **telephone and email format validation happen much later** (steps 11\u201312) \u2014 after the future-date, daily-limit, city-capacity, and household checks. So a request with a valid-looking but malformed phone/email can be rejected by a business-rule exception (e.g. household duplicate, 409) *before* its phone/email is ever validated.\n- `householdId` (step 10) is computed **before** telephone is normalized, but it only depends on `lastName` + `postcode`, so that ordering is fine. The `identityKey` duplicate check (step 13) correctly runs after telephone/email normalization.\n- `normalizeAddress` is invoked twice (once inside required-field validation, once when storing)."
